From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:32:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(colors): terminate the last OSC in the terminal sequences
 template

Local fix (not a pctrade/end4-pC backport)
Problem: sequences.txt ended its final OSC 708 with a bare ESC instead of ST (ESC \), so after applycolor.sh wrote it into a pty, kitty stayed inside that OSC string and swallowed the foreground program's output until some later ST. Neovim looked frozen, and its exit sequences (including the kitty keyboard-protocol pop) were lost, leaving the shell with doubled keystrokes.
Port: local
Drop when: the pinned sequences.txt ends with ESC \.
---
 .../.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/colors/terminal/sequences.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/colors/terminal/sequences.txt b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/colors/terminal/sequences.txt
index a677181e..c5efaecc 100644
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/colors/terminal/sequences.txt
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/colors/terminal/sequences.txt
@@ -1 +1 @@
